  id: Right_Ventricle
  partName: Right Ventricle
  descriptionChunks:
  - The ventricles are the lower chambers of the heart responsible for pumping blood
    out to the lungs and the rest of the body. The right ventricle sends deoxygenated
    blood to the lungs. Their thick muscular walls generate the force needed for
    circulation.
  - This pumping action ensures that oxygen and nutrients are delivered efficiently
    to tissues. Proper ventricular function is essential for maintaining blood pressure
    and overall cardiovascular health.
